- When several hosts share a hardware UUID, Fleet now treats exactly one of them as the device's Windows MDM host: the host that linked the device's MDM enrollment. Only that host gets the device's profiles, disk encryption status and MDM commands, Fleet doesn't enroll the other hosts in Windows MDM, and deleting one of them no longer removes the device's MDM state. On upgrade, Fleet picks one host per device, preferring the one recorded as enrolled in Fleet's MDM, and logs the other hosts sharing its hardware UUID, which are safe to delete.
